<title>GREECE: GREEK DEH-PRIVATE FIRMS TO BE ALLOWED TO PRODUCE ELECTRICITY.</title>
<headline>GREEK DEH-PRIVATE FIRMS TO BE ALLOWED TO PRODUCE ELECTRICITY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Electricity Corporation (DEH) will be allowed to form joint ventures with private firms to produce electricity, Development Minister Vasso Papandreou told a parliamentary committee.</p>
<p>The draft bill will be submitted to parliament next week, she told the committee.</p>
<p>DEH enjoys a monopoly status in producing electricity in Greece. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
